#: ../../../advanced/object_factory.md:1
msgid "Object factory"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/object_factory.md:3
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/object_factory.md:5
msgid ""
"`vtkObjectFactory` is a class in `VTK::CommonCore` module that automates the "
"instantiation of VTK objects. This allows you to write VTK scripts with the "
"same object name and having API specific classes being instantiated "
"depending on the available classes. The instantiation occurs when calling "
"the `::New()` static variable on any class deriving from `vtkObject`. "
"Therefore, `vtkNew<>` or `vtkSmartPointer<>` also follow the same logic."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/object_factory.md:7
msgid ""
"For example, after configuration, the following two lines will provide the "
"same object:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/object_factory.md:9
msgid ""
"// Creates the concrete class directly\n"
"vtkNew<vtkOpenGLRenderer> renderer1;\n"
"\n"
"// Also a vtkOpenGLRenderer\n"
"vtkNew<vtkRenderer> renderer2;\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/object_factory.md:17
msgid "Requirements"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/object_factory.md:19
msgid "CMake targets that use the VTK factory have to ensure that:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/object_factory.md:20
msgid "The module providing the override is linked"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/object_factory.md:21
msgid "That `vtk_module_autoinit` is called on the target"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/object_factory.md:23
msgid ""
"In VTK Python, the module providing the implementation needs to be imported "
"as well."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/object_factory.md:25
msgid "Add factory support to new VTK classes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/object_factory.md:27
msgid ""
"Adding support of API specific classes to the factory can be achieved in two "
"steps. The first one is to add C++ code to configure the VTK class. Then "
"some calls to CMake functions need to be done."
msgstr ""

